WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:06.500
With the "Friends" reunion special debuting
on May 27th on HBO Max, fans of the beloved

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.827
sitcom are practically buzzing with anticipation.

00:00:09.827 --> 00:00:14.150
Meanwhile, the cast has been doing promos
ahead of the special's release, including

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:18.480
a video interview with People, in which they
reflect on their time on the show and the

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:22.766
personal friendships between cast members
that have lasted throughout the years.

00:00:22.766 --> 00:00:28.179
Fans most excited for the reunion have likely
been devouring all the "Friends" reunion content

00:00:28.179 --> 00:00:32.439
they can get, which is why many of them noticed
something ... off.

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:36.420
The interview with People, which is about
eight minutes long, features all six of the

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:41.881
original cast members - Jennifer Aniston,
Courteney Cox, Lisa Kudrow, Matt LeBlanc,

00:00:41.881 --> 00:00:43.890
Matthew Perry, and David Schwimmer.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:48.899
However, of the six cast members, Perry seemed
to talk the least, remaining quiet for the

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:51.677
most part and often looking down or away.

00:00:51.677 --> 00:00:57.000
While his castmates seem jovial and animated,
Perry's demeanor is more subdued.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.444
From what little he did contribute, his speech
seemed to be off, slowed down, and somewhat slurred.

00:01:02.444 --> 00:01:07.594
Fans picked up on these details right away,
and began speculating about the actor's health.

00:01:07.594 --> 00:01:13.500
Knowing that Perry has a history with substance
abuse - including during his stint on "Friends"

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:18.110
- fans in the YouTube comments expressed their
concern about Perry possibly having recently

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:22.593
relapsed, or that he might be experiencing
depression related to his recovery.

00:01:22.593 --> 00:01:24.124
One commenter wrote,

00:01:24.124 --> 00:01:28.960
"I just wanna hug him and thank him for all
the laughter he's responsible for till this

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:31.973
very day and say how special he is."

00:01:31.973 --> 00:01:35.417
Another user, expressed similar sentiments,
writing,

00:01:35.417 --> 00:01:40.829
"I wish Matthew Perry so much solace and peace,
he's been through so much and I really appreciate

00:01:40.829 --> 00:01:42.855
him doing this appearance for us.

00:01:42.855 --> 00:01:44.969
What a blessing to have them all together."

00:01:44.969 --> 00:01:47.121
The top comment on the video reads,

00:01:47.121 --> 00:01:51.408
"I wish we could make Perry as happy as he's
made all of us."

00:01:51.408 --> 00:01:55.850
Fortunately, the cause of Perry's slurred
speech and mild demeanor is reportedly not

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:59.750
related to his addiction, but rather an unrelated
medical issue.

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:03.990
While neither Matthew Perry himself nor his
official representatives have confirmed these

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:08.649
claims, an anonymous source spoke to The Sun
about Perry's speech and appearance.

00:02:08.649 --> 00:02:12.610
The source revealed that Perry's speech was
due to an emergency dental procedure, which

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:15.839
occurred the same day that the interview with
People was filmed.

00:02:15.839 --> 00:02:19.750
Because it was of an emergency nature, the
interview couldn't have been planned around

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:24.379
his procedure, nor could proper recovery time
have been allotted beforehand.

00:02:24.379 --> 00:02:30.258
Perry’s a pro, he just had the procedure
and simply decided that the show must go on, it seems.

00:02:30.258 --> 00:02:31.790
The source told The Sun,

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:37.070
"Matthew turned up to the reunion and members
of his team said that he had an emergency

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:38.677
tooth procedure that day.

00:02:38.677 --> 00:02:42.363
That was said to impact his wellbeing and
also how he was feeling.

00:02:42.363 --> 00:02:46.480
He had been in pain from what we understand,
which caused the slurred speech."

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:50.620
The source also addressed the comments of
concern online and reiterated that,

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:55.156
"Matthew has told those around him that he
is sober, and there is no need to worry."

00:02:55.156 --> 00:02:59.690
In the past, Perry has been outspoken about
his struggle with addiction, as well as his

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:01.384
recovery and sobriety.

00:03:01.384 --> 00:03:06.000
Perry struggled with addiction to alcohol
and pills, including during his time on "Friends."

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:10.750
He has even stated publicly during an interview
with BBC Radio 2 that he doesn't remember

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:14.172
filming three full seasons of "Friends," stating,

00:03:14.172 --> 00:03:18.000
"Somewhere between season three and six ... I
was a little out of it."

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:22.826
To treat his addiction, Perry did two stints
in rehab during his time on the sitcom, in

00:03:22.826 --> 00:03:29.907
1997 and 2001, and in 2011 he returned to
rehab to continue working on his sobriety.

00:03:29.907 --> 00:03:35.260
In 2013, he told People that he turned his
former home in Malibu into a facility for

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:37.417
men's sobriety, stating,

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:42.268
"The interesting reason that I can be so helpful
to people now is that I screwed up so often.

00:03:42.268 --> 00:03:47.594
It's nice for people to see that somebody
who once struggled in their life is not struggling any more."

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:51.950
If you or someone you know is struggling with
addiction, please call the Substance Abuse

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:59.011
and Mental Health Administration's 24/7 National
Helpline at 1-800-662-HELP.

00:03:59.011 --> 00:04:03.135
That's 1-800-662-4357.

